! Lab 06: STP Root Bridge and PortFast
! Platform: Cisco Packet Tracer
! Devices: SW1 and SW2
! Purpose:
! - Understand why switching loops are dangerous
! - Understand how STP prevents loops
! - Observe STP blocking redundant links
! - Identify the STP root bridge
! - Configure SW1 as root bridge
! - Configure PortFast on PC-facing access ports
! - Verify STP operation

! Verify root bridge
show spanning-tree vlan 10

! This bridge is the root
! SW1 is now the STP root bridge for VLAN 10
! Configure PortFast on PC-facing access ports
configure terminal

interface fastEthernet 0/1
spanning-tree portfast

interface fastEthernet 0/6
spanning-tree portfast

interface fastEthernet 0/9
spanning-tree portfast

interface fastEthernet 0/19
spanning-tree portfast

end

! PortFast allows access ports to transition immediately to forwarding state
! This avoids normal STP startup delays for PCs
! Do not enable PortFast on switch-to-switch trunk links

! Verify STP operation on SW1

show spanning-tree

! Save configuration
write memory

